        {
          "id": 3093086379,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "No, well it could in theory. But what if one exists, but the other is in a different case. It would not handle differences then, as it simply would resolve to a simple string comparison. That why we should only use it when both exist, in any other case, we should compare the absolute paths (which are cleaned by the OS stuff) and check for sensitivity.",
